{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Moses did, and Aaron, and all the congregation of the children of Israel, to the Levites.</b> Our master Moses, peace be upon him, would stand the Levites upright, as it is written, ״והעמדת את הלוים לפני אהרן ולפני בניו״, and Aaron would wave them, as it is written, ״והניף אהרן את הלוים תנופה לפני ה'״. And this waving was that Aaron would take each and every one of the Levites and lift him slightly off the ground and wave him; and through this Aaron became renowned for great might and awesome strength, that he waved the Levites — who were 22,000 — in a single day, he alone. Or this was by way of a miracle, Aaron being a man of mercy, included from חסד and גבורה, for such was his form; and this is what is written (Malachi 2): ״בשלום ובמישור הלך אתי״; and therefore he was chosen in the form of the ox, of which it is written (Ezekiel 1): ״ופני שור מהשמאל״, and he would atone for the sins of Israel committed from the side of the north. And Israel would lean their hands upon the Levites, as it is written, ״וסמכו בני ישראל את ידיהם על הלוים״. And behold, for all of them there was an act of miracle in the matter."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:52.947552836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}